{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35500-what-says-wraith-to-you","id":35500,"title":"What says Wraith to you?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T04:33:56-08:00","id":35500,"title":"What says Wraith to you?","content":"Here's a question I've been pondering. it may have to do with mood, but I'd like to ask Primarily Story Tellers about their influences when they run Wraith games for their players. I've only ever participated briefly and never run my own. I guess my question is what influences you in modern media. Not necessarily what gets you in the mood, but what paints a wraithly picture for you visually or audibly. One example is say Silent Hill games or movie where you go &quot;OH! that's totally how I picture the Near Shadowlands now.&quot; Or &quot;That movie has totally given me my next hook for my Wraith game.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess why I'm asking is because even though I'm a big horror buff I just don't find many movies or books that give me that jive to imagine it playing out in the Wraith setting. The exception being cultural real world histories and documentaries about funeral rites and whatnot, but those do not equate to the Wraith game. A lot of my favorite movies could be seen as the work of Haunters and be translated into Wraith terms, but it doesn't go any father into the shadowlands that the creepy face on the other side of the mirror. All kinds of movies with ghosts in them, but they're not Wraith.<br /> <br /> Rich, if you're looking, it'd be cool to know what helped influence you when you created Wraith? (besides &quot;our Town&quot; and The Theogony of Hesiod and anything else in the <b>suggested:</b> part of the Wraith corebook)<br /> <br /> So I'm hoping some of you out there have a better knack for picking out stuff from modern media that matches how you picture the Wraith setting, or stories that you find translating easily into Wraith 'life'.<br /> <br /> For me, knowing what I know about ancient history and perception of the dead I think muddies how to imagine the Wraith setting. I'm having trouble suspending my disbelief. I'm biased and I need help from the rest of you out there to trump what I know and help me find the fodder to imagine the Wraith setting as you see it.<br /> <br /> PS: Sometimes I'm really crappy at explaining things, so maybe this request makes no sense. Feel free to say so and I'll try and explain myself better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  fixed typos 12-26-2013, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T06:24:49-08:00","id":35532,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Here\u2019s my list of Wraithly-inspiration, in no particular order of importance (or other organization).<br /> <br /> <i>City of Lost Children</i> (Caro and Jeunet, 1995)<br /> The \u201clab\u201d would be fitting as a Hierarch\u2019s office or the backdrop of a Harrowing.<br /> <br /> <i>Constantine</i> (Lawrence, 2005)<br /> Opinion: Horrible movie. Now that\u2019s out of the way\u2026<br /> There is a scene in which Neo delves into Hell so he can find the dead something or other of someone (I didn\u2019t really pay attention).<br /> The important part!<br /> When he gets to Hell, it looks like a hellfire-blasted reflection of our world. Minus some flames, I\u2019ve used this scene as a cornerstone for referencing the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> <i>The Frighteners</i> (Jackson, 1996)<br /> If you\u2019ve seen it, you know what I mean.<br /> <br /> <i>Sleepy Hollow </i>(Burton, 1999)<br /> The Horseman is a great example of dramatic use of the Embody Arcanos.<br /> <br /> The Mad Max Movies (Miller)<br /> Post-apocalyptic movies in general are a great source of inspiration. In a sense, everyone in Wraith has gone through the end of the world. Their ends, at least. <br /> The first film, <i>Mad Max</i> (Miller, 1979), has a good tone for population \u2013 you get a sense of things starting to break down \u2013 a good Wraithly sense of desoloation/isolation.<br /> <br /> <i>Beetlejuice</i> (Burton, 1980)<br /> Like <i>The Frighteners</i>, if you\u2019ve seen it, you know what I mean. The cartoon series is also good.<br /> <br /> Resident Evil Movies<br /> I hate all these movies. Mostly because (IMO) they don\u2019t make any sense. But that\u2019s alright, because we\u2019re taking all their weird crap and making our own story out of it. The stuff that doesn\u2019t make sense is still okay to use \u2013 Underworld physics doesn\u2019t have to make sense. The best Harrowings are the ones I ran without a sense of logic (although I still had purpose and structure, mind you).<br /> <br /> <i>What Dreams May Come</i> (Ward, 1998)<br /> Both frightening and hopeful. Good dead-folk stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T23:48:28-08:00","id":36195,"title":"","content":"A few random thoughts:<br /> <br /> I have a bookcase full of &quot;true&quot; ghost stories and local supernatural folklore. Read enough and you see patterns emerge on what folks think is waiting on the other side - and what might keep you hanging around post-mortem<br /> Read Thomas Ligotti - especially stories like &quot;The Red Tower&quot; and &quot;The Frolic&quot;, then follow it up with Gormenghast and a few books on architectural strangeness of the ancient world. Derinkyu, Petra, Mt. Nemrut, the Paris catacombs and the ruins of Herculaneum. Read Graham Hancock, even - just don't take his conclusions seriously. What matters is the sense of epic, crumbling grandeur. <br /> Try a Swedish band called Gosta Berlings Saga, especially the Detta Har Hant album. Mix it with some of Mark Snow's soundtrack work, especially the music he wrote for Millennium.<br /> Check out a PSN game called Rain. Chase it, if you can, with Eternal Darkness and installments in the Fatal Frame series. Alan Wake and Amnesia might also be good inspiration.<br /> <br /> Deadguy out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T14:12:36-08:00","id":36550,"title":"","content":"Some more wonderful ghost movies not yet mentioned:<br /> The Lovely Bones<br /> The Others<br /> The Devil's Backbone<br /> The Orphanage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T16:23:49-08:00","id":37058,"title":"","content":"Early chapters of Bleach","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1411-wingnut2292","name":"wingnut2292","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1411_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T17:16:05-08:00","id":37075,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, <i>The World Ends With You</i> is like a less bleak, more hip, Japanese take on Wraith. It's certainly influenced my Geist games.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wingnut2292</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35500-what-says-wraith-to-you?p=37058#post37058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Early chapters of Bleach</div> </div> </div> </div>Come to think of it, the earliest bits of <i>Yu Yu Hakusho</i> were similar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T18:20:58-08:00","id":37092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35500-what-says-wraith-to-you?p=37075#post37075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, <i>The World Ends With You</i> is like a less bleak, more hip, Japanese take on Wraith. It's certainly influenced my Geist games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man I haven't played that in so long. Gonna have to play it again soon. But yeah <i>The World Ends With You</i> does have some interesting ideas for wraith. Joshua would make for a great enigmatic Ferryman/ancient wraith.<br /> <br /> As for <i>Bleach </i>and<i> Yu Yu Hakusho</i> while they have some potential to be mined I honestly don't see too much for WtO, for a more action oriented Orpheus, GtSE and KotE games I can see it but not so much for WtO. There are similar concepts but <i>Bleach </i>and <i>Yu Yu</i> tend to be more basic in handling those concepts. Though I will admit <i>Bleach's</i> Hueco Mundo, the realm of the hollows, does remind me of WtO's Underworld. And to be fair there aren't many anime/manga series I can think of at the moment that really conveys the ideas and concepts of WtO. I vaguely remember one or two but I can't name them at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T22:36:57-08:00","id":37173,"title":"","content":"The Pixies, Sorry but think about songs like &quot;Wave of Mutilation.&quot; &quot;Where is My Mind.&quot; and &quot;In Heaven&quot;,<br /> when i listen to certain songs i feel as if they were actual stories going through, Whenever i listen to &quot;Ghosts N Stuff&quot; by deadmau5 i imagine the story of someone who died and is trying to go back to the land of the living to say goodbye to his girlfriend.<br /> <br /> &quot;Rape Me.&quot; by nirvana, i imagined as a song from a wraith fighting his Shadow,this one sending flashbacks and bringing memories to the wraith, &quot;Heart Shaped Box.&quot; to me its a mix bag of random thoughts of a wraith trying to remember his past life as well randoms lines shoot by his Shadow.<br /> <br /> as for books, I LOVE Clive Barker's Book of Blood (The Story), to me its a representation of how Desperated are the wraiths in order to make contact.<br /> <br /> The same goes for the hell on constantine (though i picture it more as Malfeas)<br /> The Crow, i guess no explanation there...same with the comic.<br /> <br /> And funny enough, to me the path of a wraith is the inverse to the one that dante had to do. Instead of going To Hell, a wraith is trying to drag himself Out to reach the skinlands...just a funny comparasion<br /> <br /> but to me wraith, as a game master. its about hope.<br /> i recently broke up a very important relationship and i found the book (or the book found me), to me its about accepting the past, learn from it, love the beautiful moments, have hope for the future, learn to let go and finally trascend in a more literal way perhaps.<br /> <br /> Funny, to me the book has worked as a therapy...ironic how some of the DMs i know have told me that the game is incredibly depressive, but on my end..it helped me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T05:06:51-08:00","id":37275,"title":"","content":"I find all of these examples really interesting and I hope I can find the time to explore them all. Thank you very much and anyone else reading Please throw your suggestions out there.<br /> <br /> I personally have a lot of ghost movies and while I can't say I've seen any ghosts in my conscious life I find all the stories of experiences that other people have had with shit they can't explain very very intriguing. I have to say that from the amount of ghost stories people have and movies about ghosts, Wraith just doesn't seem to have very much of that material. It's a Part of Wraith, sure... but not a huge part. One thing I've found in reading and watching shows with ghost stories or why Ghost hunters feel the need to go running around in the dark trying to talk to things they can't hear or explain things they feel but can't see; it all seems to boil down to wanting to know what happens when we die. What waits for us on the other side. There is a lot of hope in their stories because they really want to know if the people they've loved might be waiting for them or that someone they've lost is ok and in a better place. There's the hope that the goodness they've believed in all their lives can be reached when they cross over.<br /> <br /> And well According to Wraith, it's all BS. Granted not every person who dies will become a wraith. There's certain conditions. Certain bonds that hold a soul back. The Wraith then has to resolve these Fetters in order to Transcend and their journey then stems from the despair of being dead and confused as all get out to finding the way to let go and move on. So yeah... it does have hope, but that is mainly through the Shadowlands and not a great deal with the Skinlands unless the ST chooses to focus the game that way. For all the interaction with the living that makes for such great Ghost stories, Wraith to me doesn't seem to be about explaining the other side of those stories. So I can't relate Wraith as a setting to some of my favorite movies like Poltergeist or House on Haunted Hill, or The Eye (the original Japanese version). Maybe some of you out there can totally explain how to relate Wraith terms to those movies, but I just couldn't make those connections. The ghost stories just do not seem to have any connection to the Wraith system. Not in the way I can watch a Vampire movie and assign clan labels, or watch a movie with werewolves and relate the folklore to a First change storyline.<br /> <br /> Another thing I find confusing and frustrating is that the state of the Shadowlands has so much range of location and meaning and depth, with all their horror and danger and strife with all the souls within them, that it really parallels incredibly closely with the many cultural ideas of Hell, And not even in a Fiery demon pitchfork sort of way that it might as well drop the pretense and be Hell because that's what the corruption of the system has made it despite Charon's good intentions. In that sense if it was a hell I can totally picture that. Definitely the type of place from those scenes in the movie Constantine, Tempest winds and all. Maybe not as hot, but definitely the dark and decrepit reflection of the world of the living. It's unforgiving, it's cruel, it's filled with the souls of people used as furniture and weapons and coin. It's a place of bleakness and misery where salvation is a distant glimmer many strive to hold on to and few find true redemption. So call it what it is. Hell.<br /> <br /> So this is why I'm having trouble wrapping my brain around Wraith's setting interaction and even the movies and subject matter I thought would make things more inspired and paint out that picture for me have not worked. Again, thank you for all your help and keep the suggestions coming. I really appreciate you guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  typos again.. 12-26-2013, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T04:22:16-08:00","id":39306,"title":"","content":"Just saw the movie Wristcutters. Has anyone else seen this? Definitely an interesting and weird take on purgatory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T13:59:21-08:00","id":39569,"title":"","content":"Lovely Bones is great. <br /> <br /> I actually really like Full Metal Achemist. The perspective of 'the other side' and 'the gate' as well as equivalent exchange and the mutability of objects can be useful for perspective.<br /> <br /> Dresden Files are a great series of books with a consistent version of ghosts.<br /> <br /> I really liked the first Ghost Rider for showing spirits fighting and simply, Constantine is a fun movie (if not kind of rough).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T14:08:11-08:00","id":39575,"title":"","content":"To elaborate on an earlier post; The World Ends With You is a game about dead people given a second shot; if they can survive the week-long Reaper's Game, they can come back to life. Before they can participate, whatever they find most valuable is taken from them as an 'Entry Fee' - one characters loses their memory entirely, another loses his sister's relationship with him, things like that - to be returned to them upon victory. They occupy a plane of existence known as the Underground, which is much like the Shadowlands, and cannot be seen by the living.<br /> <br /> It's a great game, and the stories it tells all focus on interpersonal relationships. It makes good inspiration for looking at how the dead interact with their Passions, and also happens to just be all-around great. Fantastic soundtrack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}